# KiCad-derived files: artifacts, backups, and machine-local state.
#
# Source files ARE committed (symbol/footprint libs, schematics, boards,
# project settings, library tables). Everything below is regenerable from the
# sources above (backups, history, plotted outputs) or machine/user-specific
# (project-local cache, editor locks), so it must not land in git. k33p stores
# these as content-addressed artifacts instead of committing them.

# KiCad auto-restore snapshots (created on crash/recovery)
_restore_backup_*/

# KiCad "project history" — per-project mini git repositories with save history
.history/

# Project-local cache of resolved library refs + editor settings (regenerated
# on open, path-specific to the machine)
*.kicad_prl

# Editor lock files
*.lck

# Autosave scratch files
*.autosave
*~